meta {
  name: Signup
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/public/countries/{{countryCode}}/user/signup
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "someone@example.com",
    "password": "a-strong-password",
    "firstName": "Ana",
    "lastName": "Silva",
    "remember": true
  }
}

docs {
  Creates an **unvalidated** USER and emails an 8-digit code. This does NOT log
  you in — the response carries no token/cookie. Next step: **Verify Email**.

  New signups are always role USER + unvalidated, so `login` will reject them
  until verified. To create an admin instead, use `npm run create-admin`.

  Requires the anonymous session first (run **Get Anonymous Session**).

  Local dev — read the emailed code straight from KV:
  `npx wrangler kv key get "someone@example.com" --binding VALIDATION_KV --local`
}
